# Product ownership

- The user's learning vision is owned by ChatGPT agents. Build Learn as a
  distinct, first-class workspace alongside the existing PDF reader, following
  the user's analogy of Cursor IDE and Cursor Agents.
- Another agent owns the existing PDF-reader/base-product work. ChatGPT agents
  must not independently modify its rendering, reader interactions, reader
  layout, launch-facing website or unrelated base-product behavior. Report
  issues to that workstream instead of expanding Learn tasks to fix them.
- Reading PDFs, inspecting original source pages and providing source review
  within Learn remain part of the learning scope.
- Shared app entry points, document persistence, model/provider configuration
  and common design components are integration boundaries. Coordinate changes
  with the other workstream and keep them limited to the agreed Learn need.
  Preserve existing reader behavior and concurrent changes.
- Carry this ownership boundary into delegated tasks. Keep code, tests and
  repository evaluation reports authoritative; use Linear as the work register.
